  "question": {
    "text": "A convex lens made of glass (refractive index $=1.5$ ) has focal length 24 cm in air. When it is totally immersed in water (refractive index $=1.33$ ), its focal length changes to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "79GI0",
      "text": "24 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uSxJo",
      "text": "96 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ulSwp",
      "text": "48 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tdTlq",
      "text": "72 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{8}=\\left(\\frac{\\mu_{\\ell}}{\\mu_{\\mathrm{s}}}-1\\right)\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right] \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{24}=(1.5-1)\\left[\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}}\\right] ...(i)\\\\\n& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}}=\\left(\\frac{1.5}{1.33}-1\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}}\\right) \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}}=\\left(\\frac{1.5 \\times 3}{4}-1\\right) \\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}}...(ii)\n\\end{aligned}$\n(i) divided by (ii)\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}}{24}=4 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}=96 \\mathrm{~cm}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
